# Line endings are part of the measurement in this repository.
#
# The corpus is pinned by checksum in corpus/MANIFEST.sha256. Git for Windows
# installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. The scores would not move — Path.read_text() opens in universal-newlines
# mode, so the pipeline never sees a \r — but the bytes on disk change, and
# tools/verify_corpus.py would report CHANGED on a clean clone. That is the damage:
# a pin that cries wolf on every Windows machine teaches people to delete the
# manifest, which is exactly how a real corpus swap goes unnoticed in October.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the general rule goes first.

* text=auto

corpus/*.txt           text eol=lf
corpus/MANIFEST.sha256 text eol=lf

*.pdf binary
